<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! The genesis island ~ how one artifact gets built, and why the builder holds no doctrine

Every peer boots from one content-addressed genesis artifact, and the artifact carries the engine
that deserializes it. This room owns the BUILD of that artifact: what the runner reads off a disk,
what it declares about each blob, and what it refuses to decide.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/three-layers`>>

!! Three layers, and the middle one touches no disk

# ''A reads.'' The node runner walks the TW5 core script, the vendored plugin JSONs and their build
attestations off the filesystem and assembles `GenesisInputs`.
# ''B builds.'' `buildGenesisDoc(inputs)` in mesh constructs the Automerge doc. Platform-neutral by
construction — it takes bytes and returns a document, so a browser vessel and a node vessel fold the
SAME artifact from the same inputs.
# ''C writes.'' The runner lands the plain-data seed (`seed.json`) and the CAS entries. The three
region CIDs ride inside the seed as witness tiddlers, and the Automerge bytes stay an in-memory
verification witness.

''The split carries the portability.'' A build step that reached for `fs` inside layer B would bind the
artifact's shape to one host, and every host must agree on the artifact exactly.

''What does NOT belong here.'' Corpus memes load at runtime through the bag store's recipe stack, and
the runtime document urls each vessel keeps (its crossroads pointer in its own catalog; the live system documents in
the Kahu realm's registrations) never enter the island. Neither counts as genesis material: the vessel carries the first as
content and discovers the second as state.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-declaration`>>

!! A blob's class gets DECLARED at the mint, never read off its path

Each vendored file arrives as one of three classes, and `collectPlugins` decides which by READING it:

* ''grammar'' — the required memetic-wikitext plugin, matched by its own URI. One file, and the whole
of kāhuli's fast ratchet.
* ''plugin'' — a file whose JSON envelope declares a `title`. The checked-in plugin directory holds the boot set alone, and the collector packs every top-level JSON it
finds there; an operator's own collection travels as a signed offering through `nexus publish`, never baked in.
* ''base'' — the default, and what an envelope-less tiddler array or an unparseable file stands as.
The `lararium-boot-shadows` seed lives here, beside the lares/lararium bags.

''The default falls to base, the safe direction.'' A file that declares nothing gets the class
that ratchets nothing; only a file that DECLARES a plugin envelope becomes a plugin. An unparseable blob takes the
same road rather than failing the build, because it declared nothing either.

''The class rides INTO the descriptor,'' so verification classifies exactly as the mint did. A gate
that re-derived the class from a path would stand as a second reader, free to disagree with the first — the
[[carrier gradient|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/carrier-gradient]] lesson, one layer down.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/regions`>>

!! Three regions, two ratchets

The build prints three CIDs and seals each into the seed as a witness tiddler, and they never read as
three tiers of one thing:

|!Region |!What it folds |!What advancing it means |
|`engineCid` |the TW5 core — the hearth true-name |the SLOW ratchet; it re-binds membership mesh-wide and rides inside every signed device-delegation preimage |
|`grammarCid` |the required grammar ALONE |marked to RETIRE — the grammar holds no versions (kahu#/contract); retirement owed in code, pending a scout's measurement of its consumers |
|`pluginsCid` |the plugin-class blobs the bake packs — neither the grammar nor the base seed |a REGION, never a kāhuli tier — an operator's own offerings travel by `nexus publish`, and plugin drift never counts as grammar drift |

''The engine's preimage follows no region fold.'' `computeEngineCid` takes the core digest alone, so no
version label can reach the preimage; the other two fold their sorted `{id, sha256}` pairs under their OWN
domain literal. Three hand-written folds read like an inconsistency and enact the separation.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/determinism`>>

!! The actor seed makes two builds the same build

`actorSeed = sha256hex` over the inputs the bake packs, each plugin blob labelled by its path within the
repo, so two builds of one commit, from any checkout location, produce identical seed and CAS bytes. Automerge
would otherwise stamp a fresh actor per build, and two byte-identical inputs would fold to two different
artifacts, leaving the artifact useless as a name.

''The kupono law: the seed folds only what every Lararium shares and boots alike.'' It folds the engine
core, the plugin blobs the bake packs (every one boots in every vessel's islands) and the attestation the
bake reads. Nothing per-operator or per-place reaches it: no working copy under `bags/`, no draft, no file
standing on one machine alone. The `bags/` carriers hold the operator's working copies of what later
becomes public or crossroads material; genesis carries none of them, and a seed that folded them would
move `seedCid`, a name every Lararium reads, on one operator's private edit. One function names the
packed set (`genesisPackedPluginFiles`), and the bake's collector and the seed both read it, so the two
cannot drift.

''An attestation that disagrees with its blob ABORTS the build.'' A plugin whose recorded
`pluginJsonSha256` misses the bytes on disk throws rather than vendoring; a half-true genesis costs more
than none, because every vessel downstream would carry the lie by hash.

<<~/ahu>>

